Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:20:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] drm/imagination: apple: Stop firmware before releasing
 its pages

Driver removal freed firmware storage while the DMA writer still ran.
Stop firmware and pollers before releasing pages, and defer an idle
firmware restart until a job needs it. A blocked submit ioctl also held
reboot in DRM unplug SRCU for minutes. Quiesce hardware in shutdown
without unplug or scheduler flush. Bound submit locking and engine waits,
cancel fences with -ESHUTDOWN, and use terminal-only non-joining work,
mailbox and runtime-PM operations. Preserve the existing power requests
and force-stop writes. Retain callback storage until CPUs stop; ordinary
teardown still joins workers.

Affects: Apple A9 and A10 firmware teardown and reboot
Assisted-by: LLM
